fuerat, colonias deducit.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eus. a. pr.</HI></P> <P COM="0063">124 Justinus <NOTE N="(22*)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063D"></COL> Eusebius  <HI REND="ITALIC">Justum</HI>  eum appellat. ad an. 120.</NOTE> , episcopus Alexandriae, sedit annis
XI;  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. a.</HI>  122.—Adrianus legem dedit Atheniensibus.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Eus. a. pr.; def. in B.</HI></P> <P COM="0063">125 Hierosolymis post Philippum <NOTE N="(23)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063D"></COL> Zachaeum secuti sunt Tobias, Benjamin,
Joannes, Mathias, Philippus, Seneca, hunc Justus II.
Levi, Ephrem, Joseph, Judas II, omnes ex Judaeis.</NOTE>  Seneca decimus
